            "review_title": "Review at The Tavern",
            "review_text": "Abrie Theart\n1 contribution\n1\nFelt like home!\nSep 2019\nAfter (only) two weeks from home (South Africa) I felt like some \"western\" food. Spesifically the method of preparing food and herbs/sauces and presentation. (I had enough noodles and rice for a while) This was the one stop have it all. Besides the layout (Smoking and non smoking area - upper and lower floor, a bar counter and draught machines, country flags agianst the ceiling, ouside tables as well, very good male and femail toilets, pleasent and friendly waiters, and an outstanding menu, with about everything a \"westerner\" will desire, including drinks and cocktails. The best part about was the music they played - some lekker ouldies and the admosphere of english speaking folk and laughter was absolute comforting. Prising was reasonable and I gladly give a 10% tip. This was in the afternoon - an you imagine late afternoons and evening. Oh yeah, there were pool, eating big sizes of stake and drinking competition from certian hours. (anytime, the whole time) Manger came to greet us and even overed us something on the house. Guys... do yourself a favour and visit the place, but rather go with Grabcar. You might enjoy it to much to drive or bike!. Thank you to Manager and Staff of The tavern! I will visit soon!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 11, 2019",
